From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yugidraft <yugidraft@localhost>
Date: Sun, 6 Feb 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] core: fix the n > 2 summon-to-opponent, old-rule summon oath
 and pass loop sites in operations and processor

All changes are new code for n_duelists > 2. With 2 duelists every line is the stock code.

Pass loops (TrapMonsterAdjust, ChangePos): the loop counted the passes done and compared them with the number of
living duelists. A duelist who was done and was eliminated later was counted, so the loop ended one duelist early. The
count is now a mask (pass_mask), the same method as the PhaseEvent pass record. The loop ends when every living duelist
has its bit. The ChangePos start code ran again at every pass and reset the pass player to the reason player, so every
pass was for the same duelist. The start code now runs once (pass_player starts as DUELIST_NONE).

Summon to the opponent's field (EFFECT_FLAG_SPSUM_PARAM with o_range): Summon, MSet and SpSummonRule used "1 - player".
At seat 2 or 3 that is not a seat. Now the monster goes to the first living opponent in turn order for whom the summon
works, the same rule as card::check_summon_procedure. If none works, the first living opponent.

EFFECT_OPPO_CHOOSES_SPSUMMON_ZONE: the chooser is the first living opponent of the chooser so far.

Old-rule summon oaths (DUEL_CANNOT_SUMMON_OATH_OLD, DUEL_SPSUMMON_ONCE_OLD_NEGATE) in AddChain and Chain step 5: the
"other" summon player of a CATEGORY_SPECIAL_SUMMON with PLAYER_ALL is the first living opponent of the summon player.
op_param that is not a duelist is the triggering player. The group is read only as far as it goes.
SpSummon step 2 no longer indexes the once set with a summon player that is not a duelist.

DUEL_1_FACEUP_FIELD (the two sites in the Chain process): the Field Spell of every other living duelist is disabled or destroyed.

Player values from a script that are not a duelist seat (all_id, a seat above the table, 1 - tp at seat 2 or 3):
process(Draw), Damage, Recover, DiscardDeck, TossCoin, TossDice and DiscardHand now do nothing (result 0).
DiscardDeck had no guard and read player[255]. send_to and destroy send a card to its owner when the player
is not a duelist.

Sites that stay as they are: every other opponent_of in operations.cpp, processor.cpp and processor_unit.h is
inside an n_duelists == 2 branch or behind an earlier n > 2 branch.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
